WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.000
I want to start today talking about Florida.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:08.540
And yeah, in a certain sense, this is a story
about Ron DeSantis, but it is really a story

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:16.170
about Ron DeSantis as governor, not Ron DeSantis
as the maybe future failed Republican presidential

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:19.950
primary candidate Ron DeSantis, who still,
as of this moment, has not announced that

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:23.200
he is running against Donald Trump in that
Republican primary.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:32.809
I want to show you the texture of the right
wing hellscape that DeSantis is rapidly transforming

00:00:32.809 --> 00:00:34.530
Florida into now.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:40.350
Full disclosure, I know people e-mailing,
but David, you say these things about Florida

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:42.379
and then you go to Florida.

00:00:42.379 --> 00:00:43.510
Okay.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:47.460
I also said things that are terrible about
Donald Trump, but I lived in the United States

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:48.730
when Trump was president.

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:53.609
So, yes, there are parts of Florida that I
think are great, even though they have infrastructure

00:00:53.609 --> 00:00:59.769
problems as a result of of Ron DeSantis and
right wing state policy, those liberal parts

00:00:59.769 --> 00:01:05.470
of Florida with the good restaurants, as Alex
Jones would say, yeah, I frequently go there

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:10.570
and I don't understand how that devalues in
any way the criticism of the policy that the

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.280
Santos has put in place.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:15.939
So CNN recently had this list that they put
up.

00:01:15.939 --> 00:01:17.350
Let's take a look at it.

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:24.260
In recent times, Ron DeSantis has signed a
six week abortion ban, ended concealed weapons

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:25.270
permits.

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:31.130
The requirement for such permits ban gender
affirming care for trans youth.

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:37.899
Restricted drag shows expanded the don't say
gay law blocked and an advanced placement

00:01:37.899 --> 00:01:44.400
African-American studies curriculum class
and prohibited vaccine mandates.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:48.060
First of I am going to make two arguments
to you here.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:53.250
First argument, all of these bills and laws
are terrible ideas.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:02:01.000
And number two, many of them also directly
contradict the stated values of low government

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:07.600
intervention, little government involvement,
freedom and liberty that they claim to espouse.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.009
So let's go through some of these six week
abortion ban.

00:02:11.009 --> 00:02:15.769
DeSantis signed that in a closed door ceremony,
I believe it was last month.

00:02:15.769 --> 00:02:21.200
The bill prohibits physicians from performing
abortions after six weeks into a pregnancy

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.520
in most cases.

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:29.890
As I've explained before, many women don't
even know they're pregnant until the six week

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:30.890
mark.

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:37.420
Because when you've missed your period, if
you are pregnant, you're basically five weeks

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:43.930
pregnant for five, depending on who you ask
or, you know, the particulars of that.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:49.459
So it is completely unrealistic, absolutely
unreasonable.

00:02:49.459 --> 00:02:51.670
And it is close to a full abortion ban.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:56.510
It also says that if you want an exception
because you've been raped, you have to provide

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:59.100
evidence of the rape.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:00.629
Okay.

00:03:00.629 --> 00:03:06.310
If it's the result of incest or human trafficking,
you need to provide evidence and that only

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:09.600
gets you an exception up to 15 weeks.

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:16.280
This is if Roe v Wade were still in place,
it would blatantly violate Roe v Wade.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:20.450
It's another attempt to control women's bodies
and limit choices.

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:22.870
And it is insane.

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:24.260
Government overreach.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:27.800
We have the bill that lets you concealed carry
without a permit.

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:28.800
Okay.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:31.230
DeSantis signed this also last month.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:39.650
This allows gun owners to carry firearms in
public without any additional permitting or

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:41.780
training required.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:47.209
And it also ends the state requirement that
when you leave your home with a concealed

00:03:47.209 --> 00:03:52.020
weapon, you must have special training or
even special training, I think is what we

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:53.180
would call it.

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:55.220
It's a gift to the gun lobby.

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:57.379
It's a gift to the NRA.

00:03:57.379 --> 00:03:59.870
It's a gift to the more guns in more places.

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:02.769
And it will make Florida less safe.

00:04:02.769 --> 00:04:07.430
It will make Florida more prone to gun violence
and accidents.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:14.379
We then have this package of five bills that
were passed and signed into law by Ron DeSantis.

00:04:14.379 --> 00:04:20.900
And here we are talking about a lot of bills
that relate directly to the rights of the

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:22.830
LGBT community.

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:28.380
And here we're talking about a ban on gender
affirming care for trans youth.

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:34.580
This will prevent doctors from providing hormone
therapy or surgery to minors who identify

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:35.600
as trans.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:41.770
You could argue that it is a form of denial
of medical care, that you're just you're taking

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:46.210
away medical freedom, because what we're talking
about here is saying, hey, here's people who

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:52.900
may need certain services as determined by
medical professionals instead.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:56.880
You have some Republican lawmakers saying
you're not going to be allowed to do it.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:58.880
Restrictions on drag shows.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:03.919
This is a law that will prohibit any establishment
that serves alcohol from hosting performances

00:05:03.919 --> 00:05:06.490
by drag queens or drag kings.

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:11.180
You can argue that this is discrimination
against a form of artistic expression.

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:16.140
You can argue this violates free speech because
at the end of the day, we're not talking about

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:21.110
grooming or pedophilia or sexual assault or
any of the things that they love to say are

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:24.229
inextricable from drag shows.

00:05:24.229 --> 00:05:26.850
It's a form of expression and it's a government
banning that.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:28.370
We will see what happens.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:30.900
There's the expansion of don't say gay.

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:36.990
Don't say gay prohibits teachers from discussing
sexual orientation or gender identity.

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:38.220
Except does it.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:43.650
Are you allowed to say as a female teacher,
Oh, my male husband.

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:47.260
Well, that is a discussion of gender identity.

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:50.400
But that's not bad because we know what the
real point of it is.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:59.000
It's to censor and silence LGBT voices, experiences
and the reality that all sorts of different

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:02.430
types of people exist in our society and culture.

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:08.680
There's the bill in addition to this, which
we talked about before, that blocks the Advanced

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:13.310
Placement African-American studies class from
being offered in public schools.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:18.550
Remember, they framed it as they are forcing
this indoctrination onto our children.

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:22.440
It's an optional class, in my experience.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:25.840
It's not as though advanced placement classes.

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:27.970
Are exactly super popular.

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:29.580
I mean, they often fill.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:33.540
But what I mean is it's not like the entire
school is you're looking to take these classes.

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:35.720
It's a whitewashing of history.

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:39.430
It denies many of the struggles of black Americans.

00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:41.340
And we've talked about it before.

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:48.960
And then lastly, a bill that bans any vaccine
mandates by any entity in Florida that includes

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:52.370
businesses, schools and government agencies.

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:59.240
Now, whatever your feelings are about a COVID
vaccine requirement, and I'm there with you,

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:05.810
if indeed the COVID vaccine doesn't prevent
transmission, there is a case to say it shouldn't

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:06.810
be required.

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:12.180
The counter would be if it reduces the chance
of hospitalization and death.

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:13.470
For military readiness.

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:15.099
It certainly seems like it could make a difference.

00:07:15.099 --> 00:07:18.840
But my point is step back from the COVID vaccine.

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:24.099
Think about how reckless and irresponsible
it is to say you can't have any vaccine requirements,

00:07:24.099 --> 00:07:32.020
that you can't have any vaccine mandates when
we have so many vaccines that do prevent transmission

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:35.270
and are quite literally public health.

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:42.349
God sense, there's probably some better word
I could use that's less religiously oriented.

00:07:42.349 --> 00:07:49.139
These are bills that are harmful to Floridians,
but they're also harmful to democracy.

00:07:49.139 --> 00:07:55.180
And many of them run directly counter to the
stated values that these Republicans claim

00:07:55.180 --> 00:08:00.139
to espouse, which is they say freedom, liberty,
do whatever you want government only involved

00:08:00.139 --> 00:08:01.139
when absolutely necessary.

00:08:01.139 --> 00:08:02.910
Freedom of speech, freedom of expression.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:08.780
Except, well, no drag shows and no doctors
and patients deciding what's best for them

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:10.620
and all these other things.

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:18.800
The takeaway is their principles evaporate
as soon as they conflict with the political

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:20.539
reality that they are trying to fight

